      "lineAnnotations": {
        "72": {"synopsis":"The keyboard part of INT_FRAME: INT_KEYPAD (the keypad in 128 BASIC, then KEYBOARD) with BC\nand DE kept, then the registers back and EI."},
        "74": {"comment":"The keypad, then the keyboard (INT_KEYPAD)"},
        "79": {"comment":"HL and AF back"},
        "81": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "2898": {"synopsis":"$90 and up: first OUT_NEW_TOKENS, for $A3 and $A4 (SPECTRUM and PLAY in 128 BASIC); then as\nin the 48K ROM: $90-$A4 the UDG A - $90, from UDG (OUT_CHAR_BC), $A5 and up OUT_TOKEN.","comment":"$A3/$A4 first (OUT_NEW_TOKENS)"},
        "2901": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instructions"},
        "2902": {"comment":"A = the UDG's number","synopsis":"A UDG: A + $15 is its number, $00-$14 (OUT_NEW_TOKENS comes here with A - $A5)."},
        "2904": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "2905": {"comment":"BC = UDG"},
        "3095": {"synopsis":"PRINT_ENTRY after FIND_ENTRY: OUT_NEW_TOKENS comes here with DE at its own keyword and the\nspacing number on the stack.","comment":"A $20 or more and a letter first?"},
        "4924": {"synopsis":"Prints the report's code character (PRINT_A_DIGIT), a space, then its message; in 128 BASIC\nthe rest of the report is the other ROM's (HOOK_REPORT).","comment":"Printed"},
        "4927": {"comment":"A space"},
        "4930": {"comment":"A = the number"},
        "4931": {"comment":"The message for the number, from REPORT_MESSAGES"},
        "4937": {"comment":"Message 0, DE = COMMA_MESSAGES; or the other ROM (HOOK_REPORT)"},
        "4940": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instructions"},
        "4944": {"comment":"The line number, PPC ($FFFE for a direct command prints as 0)"},
        "4951": {"comment":"':'"},
        "4954": {"comment":"The statement number, SUBPPC"},
        "4959": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "4962": {"comment":"Empty the edit line, keeping its $0D"},
        "4965": {"comment":"Report 0: no CONTINUE position"},
        "4971": {"comment":"Reports 9 (STOP statement) and L (BREAK into program) continue after the statement"},
        "4975": {"comment":"Report L?"},
        "7037": {"synopsis":"A jump pending (NSPPC bit 7 clear)? In 128 BASIC the other ROM answers (HOOK_STMT_JUMP).","comment":"A jump pending? (HOOK_STMT_JUMP)"},
        "7040": {"comment":"Filler: the rest of the replaced instruction"},
        "7041": {"comment":"No: the next statement"},
        "7043": {"comment":"HL = NEWPPC"},
        "7046": {"comment":"Bit 15: the edit line?"},
        "7048": {"comment":"No: a program line"},
        "7156": {"synopsis":"After a statement: ENTER ends the line (LINE_END), ':' starts the next (STMT_LOOP), anything\nelse is report C. In 128 BASIC the other ROM takes over (HOOK_STMT_NEXT).","comment":"The current character, ENTER? (HOOK_STMT_NEXT)"},
        "7161": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "7166": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "9780": {"synopsis":"INKEY$: with '#' a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX, operation $1A). Otherwise, when\nrunning, the key held now as a one-character string, or an empty one (INKEY_KEYS: the\nkeyboard, and in 128 BASIC the keypad).","comment":"Priority 16, operation $5A"},
        "9783": {"comment":"Past INKEY$"},
        "9784": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "9786": {"comment":"Then a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX)"},
        "9789": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "9792": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "9794": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9798": {"comment":"The key held (INKEY_KEYS)"},
        "9801": {"comment":"C = 0: an empty string so far"},
        "9803": {"comment":"Too many keys: empty"},
        "9805": {"comment":"Its main code (KEY_MAIN_CODE)"},
        "9808": {"comment":"No key: empty"},
        "9810": {"comment":"D = $FF: bit 3 set, L mode"},
        "9811": {"comment":"E = the main code"},
        "9812": {"comment":"The key's code (KEY_DECODE, MODE 0)"},
        "9815": {"synopsis":"The key's character A as a one-character string in the workspace (INKEY_KEYS comes here\ntoo).","comment":"The character kept"},
        "9816": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "9819": {"comment":"Room for it (WORK_ROOM)"},
        "9821": {"comment":"Into the room"},
        "9822": {"comment":"C = 1: one character"},
        "14446": {"synopsis":"The frame interrupt's keys: in 128 BASIC (FLAGS bit 4 set) the keypad first (KP_KEYBOARD),\nthen the keyboard (KEYBOARD). Keeps IX."},
        "14448": {"comment":"128 BASIC?"},
        "14454": {"comment":"The keypad (KP_KEYBOARD)"},
        "14457": {"synopsis":"The keyboard (KEYBOARD).","comment":"The keyboard"},
        "14463": {"synopsis":"Sets up for the keypad line, which is the AY chip's I/O port A (register 14): C = $FD, D =\n$FF (register select, port $FFFD), E = $BF (data, port $BFFD); H = register 7, L = register\n14 with bits 4-7 set.\nChanges: A, B, C, D, E, H, L."},
        "14470": {"comment":"Register 7"},
        "14474": {"comment":"H = its value"},
        "14476": {"comment":"Register 14, the I/O port"},
        "14480": {"comment":"A = the port"},
        "14482": {"comment":"Bits 4-7 set"},
        "14486": {"synopsis":"Writes L to register 14 (the line out is its bit 0)."},
        "14487": {"comment":"Register 14 selected"},
        "14492": {"comment":"L to the data port"},
        "14495": {"synopsis":"A = register 14 (the line in is its bit 5)."},
        "14503": {"synopsis":"Bit 0 of L cleared and written (KP_PORT_WRITE): the line out low."},
        "14509": {"synopsis":"Bit 0 of L set and written (KP_PORT_WRITE): the line out high."},
        "14515": {"synopsis":"A delay of B rounds of DJNZ."},
        "14518": {"synopsis":"A delay of B x 16 rounds (KP_DELAY)."},
        "14519": {"comment":"16 rounds each"},
        "14528": {"synopsis":"Waits up to B reads for the line in (bit 5) to go low. Exit: Z when it did, NZ when it did\nnot."},
        "14533": {"comment":"Low?"},
        "14539": {"synopsis":"Returns."},
        "14540": {"synopsis":"Waits up to B reads for the line in (bit 5) to go high. Exit: NZ when it did, Z when it did\nnot."},
        "14545": {"comment":"High?"},
        "14551": {"synopsis":"Returns."},
        "14552": {"synopsis":"Reads one bit from the keypad (KP_READ_BITS with B = 1) into bit 7 of A."},
        "14559": {"synopsis":"Reads four bits from the keypad (KP_READ_BITS with B = 4) into bits 4-7 of A."},
        "14564": {"synopsis":"Reads B bits from the keypad, the first ending up lowest of them, shifted in from bit 7 of\nA: for each, the line out high, a wait for the line in to go low (KP_WAIT_LOW, $A3 reads),\nthe line out low, a delay, the line in sampled, then the line out high and low again with\ndelays.\nExit: NZ (and the keypad marked absent, KP_NO_REPLY) when the line in is low to start with\nor does not answer."},
        "14569": {"comment":"The line in high?"},
        "14571": {"comment":"No: no reply"},
        "14573": {"comment":"A = 0: the bits collected here"},
        "14574": {"synopsis":"One bit: the line out high, the answer awaited."},
        "14576": {"comment":"Line out high"},
        "14579": {"comment":"Up to $A3 reads"},
        "14584": {"comment":"No answer"},
        "14586": {"comment":"Line out low"},
        "14589": {"comment":"Past the filler"},
        "14591": {"synopsis":"Two bytes of $FF after a jump."},
        "14593": {"synopsis":"After a delay, the line in is the bit: carry set for high, clear for low."},
        "14598": {"comment":"The port"},
        "14601": {"comment":"The line in"},
        "14609": {"synopsis":"A 0 bit: carry clear."},
        "14612": {"synopsis":"The bit into A from the top; then the line out high and low again, with delays, before the\nnext bit.","comment":"Into bit 7"},
        "14632": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "14635": {"synopsis":"No answer in the middle of a bit: the stack tidied."},
        "14637": {"synopsis":"No keypad: the line out high, $5B88 = 0 (absent). Exit: A = 1, NZ, no carry."},
        "14640": {"comment":"$5B88 = 0: no keypad"},
        "14645": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "14648": {"synopsis":"Whether the keypad is there, keeping its state in $5B88 (bit 7 set: found; 0: none yet) and\na countdown in $5B89:\n1. Found already: Z and carry (KP_FOUND).\n2. The line in low: no keypad (KP_NO_REPLY).\n3. Otherwise a countdown from $4C calls (NZ and carry while it runs, KP_POLL_WAIT); at its\n   end a handshake: the line out low, the line in must go low ($21 reads), the line out\n   high, the line in must go high ($24 reads), a long delay, then four bits are read\n   (KP_READ_4BITS) and kept in bits 4-7 of $5B88 with bit 7 set: Z and no carry.\nAny step that fails is KP_NO_REPLY: NZ and no carry."},
        "14651": {"comment":"Found already?"},
        "14658": {"comment":"The line in"},
        "14663": {"comment":"Low: no keypad"},
        "14665": {"comment":"A countdown running?"},
        "14671": {"comment":"No: start one"},
        "14675": {"comment":"From $4C"},
        "14682": {"synopsis":"The countdown: one less; not yet 0, wait (KP_POLL_WAIT)."},
        "14691": {"comment":"At 0: the state cleared"},
        "14701": {"comment":"Line out low"},
        "14704": {"comment":"The line in must go low"},
        "14711": {"comment":"Line out high"},
        "14714": {"comment":"The line in must go high"},
        "14721": {"comment":"Line out low"},
        "14726": {"comment":"A long delay"},
        "14729": {"comment":"Four bits"},
        "14734": {"comment":"Kept with bit 7 set: found"},
        "14741": {"comment":"Z, no carry"},
        "14745": {"synopsis":"Found: Z and carry."},
        "14748": {"synopsis":"Not known yet: NZ and carry."},
        "14752": {"synopsis":"Reads which keypad key is held: KP_POLL, then (only when bits 7 and 6 of $5B88 are set) up\nto five 4-bit groups, each announced by a 1 bit (KP_READ_1BIT, KP_READ_4BITS), packed into\n$5B8A downwards; then the key's number from the one set bit among $5B88-$5B8A masked by\nKP_MASKS (KP_KEY_NUMBER).\nExit: Z with E = the key's code ($5A and up; $80 and up for none), or NZ (no keypad, no\nanswer, or more than one key).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; $5B88-$5B8A."},
        "14755": {"comment":"Bits 7 and 6 of $5B88 both set?"},
        "14762": {"comment":"IX = $5B8A"},
        "14766": {"comment":"Five groups"},
        "14768": {"synopsis":"One group: its announcing bit, then four bits when it is 1."},
        "14772": {"comment":"No answer"},
        "14775": {"comment":"A group follows?"},
        "14779": {"comment":"Its four bits"},
        "14786": {"comment":"C = them"},
        "14790": {"comment":"Odd group: the low half"},
        "14806": {"synopsis":"An even group: the high half."},
        "14808": {"synopsis":"Combined into the byte."},
        "14812": {"synopsis":"After an even group, the next byte down."},
        "14819": {"synopsis":"The next group."},
        "14821": {"comment":"E = $80: no key yet"},
        "14823": {"comment":"From $5B88"},
        "14827": {"comment":"HL = KP_MASKS"},
        "14830": {"comment":"Three bytes"},
        "14832": {"synopsis":"Each byte masked: a set bit is a key; E becomes its number (byte x 8 + bit), and a second\none makes it fail (KP_BAD)."},
        "14835": {"comment":"Masked"},
        "14836": {"comment":"No key here"},
        "14838": {"comment":"A key found before?"},
        "14847": {"synopsis":"Two bytes of $FF after a jump."},
        "14849": {"synopsis":"B = the byte's top bit number; the highest set bit found by shifting left."},
        "14860": {"synopsis":"One shift."},
        "14867": {"comment":"E = the key's number","synopsis":"E = the number; more set bits in the byte fail."},
        "14871": {"synopsis":"The next byte."},
        "14876": {"comment":"No key?"},
        "14880": {"comment":"Numbers from 4 up are two less"},
        "14887": {"synopsis":"Bit 3 of $5B8A set: E = (E AND $7F) + $12, the other set of codes."},
        "14900": {"synopsis":"E + $5A: the key's code. Z."},
        "14906": {"synopsis":"No answer: NZ."},
        "14908": {"synopsis":"Two keys: NZ."},
        "14911": {"synopsis":"KP_KEY_NUMBER's masks for $5B88, $5B89 and $5B8A."},
        "14914": {"synopsis":"The keypad in the frame interrupt, as KEYBOARD does for the keys (every second frame, so its\ncounts are halved):\n1. On even frames KP_SCAN; nothing more unless it gives a key code.\n2. Each KSTATE set holding a keypad code ($5B and up) counts its release counter down, and\n   is freed at 0.\n3. KP_CODE_OK must accept the code. A code a set already holds is a key still held: its\n   release counter back to 10 and its repeat counter down, REPPER / 2 again at 0\n   (KP_REPEAT). A new code goes into a free set with a release count of 10, a repeat count\n   of REPDEL / 2, and its character (KP_CODE_TO_KEY).\nA new or repeated key goes into LAST_K, with FLAGS bit 5 set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; KSTATE, LAST_K, FLAGS."},
        "14916": {"comment":"FRAMES: an odd frame?"},
        "14923": {"comment":"Even: the keypad"},
        "14927": {"synopsis":"Both KSTATE sets in turn, from KSTATE."},
        "14930": {"synopsis":"A set in use with a keypad code: its release counter down, freed at 0."},
        "14935": {"comment":"A keypad code?"},
        "14944": {"comment":"Freed"},
        "14946": {"synopsis":"The next set, until both are done."},
        "14953": {"comment":"A code the keypad may give?"},
        "14957": {"comment":"Held in the first set?"},
        "14964": {"comment":"Or the second?"},
        "14971": {"comment":"Second set free?"},
        "14975": {"comment":"Or the first?"},
        "14979": {"synopsis":"A new key into the free set: the code, a release count of 10, a repeat count of REPDEL / 2,\nits character."},
        "14982": {"comment":"Release count"},
        "14985": {"comment":"REPDEL / 2"},
        "14992": {"comment":"E = the character (KP_CODE_TO_KEY)"},
        "14996": {"synopsis":"The character into LAST_K; FLAGS bit 5 set: a new key."},
        "15006": {"synopsis":"A key still held: release count back to 10; the repeat counter down, at 0 REPPER / 2 again\nand the key repeated."},
        "15010": {"comment":"Repeat time?"},
        "15012": {"comment":"REPPER / 2"},
        "15022": {"synopsis":"Whether E is a code the keypad may give now: with $5B66 bit 0 set, below $6D; otherwise\nbelow $80 and not $6C. Exit: Z when it is."},
        "15026": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 0?"},
        "15030": {"comment":"Below $6D?"},
        "15034": {"synopsis":"Z: accepted."},
        "15036": {"synopsis":"Below $80, and not $6C."},
        "15044": {"comment":"$6C: runs through these NOPs to KP_CODE_NO"},
        "15060": {"synopsis":"NZ: refused."},
        "15063": {"synopsis":"E = the character keypad code E gives: KP_KEY_TABLE + (E - $5B), with the table's start\nchosen by the code's range (and $5B66 bit 0), so each range of codes reads its own part of\nthe table. Keeps HL."},
        "15065": {"comment":"DE = E - $5B"},
        "15073": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 0?"},
        "15082": {"synopsis":"The table start for the code's range."},
        "15100": {"comment":"Past the filler"},
        "15102": {"synopsis":"$00, $FF, $FF after a jump."},
        "15105": {"synopsis":"The last ranges."},
        "15119": {"synopsis":"E = the character."},
        "15123": {"synopsis":"KP_CODE_TO_KEY's characters, read at different starts for different ranges of codes: '.',\nENTER, '3', '2', '1', ')', '(', '*', '/', '-', '9', '8', '7', '+', '6', '5', '4', '0', then\nkeyword codes $A5 (RND), ENTER, $A6-$AA, the control codes $0B, $0C, $07, $09, $0A, $08, and\nkeyword codes $AC-$B4."},
        "15163": {"synopsis":"REPORT_CHAR's hook: in 48 BASIC (FLAGS bit 4 clear) what it replaced, A = 0 and DE =\nCOMMA_MESSAGES; in 128 BASIC the other ROM's address $010F (ROM0_JUMP)."},
        "15167": {"comment":"128 BASIC?"},
        "15169": {"comment":"No: A = 0, DE = COMMA_MESSAGES"},
        "15174": {"synopsis":"HL = $010F, then ROM0_JUMP."},
        "15177": {"synopsis":"Continues at address HL in the other ROM: HL goes on the stack in place of the return\naddress (which is left in HL), and the routine at $5B00 in RAM swaps the ROMs and returns\nthere. The hooks use $010F, $0112 and $0115.\nObserved: at the 128K's start-up menu $5B00 held code that flips bit 4 of the byte at $5B5C,\nwrites it to port $7FFD with interrupts off, and returns; FLAGS bit 4 was set there.","comment":"HL to the stack, the return address to HL"},
        "15181": {"synopsis":"STMT_JUMP's hook: in 48 BASIC what it replaced, NSPPC bit 7 tested (Z: a jump pending); in\n128 BASIC the other ROM's $0112 (ROM0_JUMP)."},
        "15192": {"synopsis":"HL = $0112, then ROM0_JUMP."},
        "15197": {"synopsis":"STMT_NEXT's hook: in 48 BASIC what it replaced, the current character compared with ENTER;\nin 128 BASIC the other ROM's $0115 (ROM0_JUMP)."},
        "15207": {"synopsis":"HL = $0115, then ROM0_JUMP."},
        "15212": {"synopsis":"INKEY$'s key: the keyboard as in the 48K ROM (READ_KEYS, KEY_MAIN_CODE, KEY_DECODE); with no\nkey, in 128 BASIC, the keypad (KP_SCAN with interrupts off, KP_CODE_OK, KP_CODE_TO_KEY). A\nkey goes to OP_INKEY_CHAR, none to OP_INKEY_STR with C = 0.","comment":"The keys held (READ_KEYS)"},
        "15215": {"comment":"C = 0: an empty string so far"},
        "15217": {"comment":"Too many keys"},
        "15219": {"comment":"Its main code (KEY_MAIN_CODE)"},
        "15222": {"comment":"No key"},
        "15224": {"comment":"D = $FF: L mode"},
        "15226": {"comment":"The key's code (KEY_DECODE)"},
        "15229": {"comment":"Stacked as a string"},
        "15232": {"synopsis":"No key: in 128 BASIC, the keypad."},
        "15236": {"comment":"48 BASIC: empty"},
        "15239": {"comment":"The keypad, interrupts off"},
        "15246": {"comment":"A code it may give?"},
        "15251": {"comment":"Its character"},
        "15258": {"synopsis":"No key: an empty string."},
        "15263": {"synopsis":"OUT_UDG_TOKEN's first step: codes $A3 and $A4 in 128 BASIC print SPECTRUM and PLAY\n(NEW_TOKEN_NAMES) through PRINT_TOKEN's printing, spaced as a keyword; anything else, and\n$A3/$A4 in 48 BASIC (where they are UDGs), goes on as in the 48K ROM: OUT_TOKEN from $A5,\nOUT_UDG below.","comment":"SPECTRUM?"},
        "15267": {"comment":"PLAY?"},
        "15271": {"synopsis":"As in the 48K ROM: a keyword from $A5 (OUT_TOKEN), a UDG below (OUT_UDG)."},
        "15279": {"synopsis":"$A3 or $A4: a keyword in 128 BASIC only."},
        "15285": {"comment":"Return to NEW_KEYWORD_END"},
        "15291": {"comment":"DE = SPECTRUM"},
        "15296": {"comment":"Or PLAY"},
        "15299": {"synopsis":"Printed with the token rule's spaces (4 on the stack: a space after), from PRINT_ENTRY's\ntest of FIND_ENTRY's carry (PRINT_ENTRY_AT)."},
        "15305": {"synopsis":"After it: on the printer (FLAGS bit 1) done; on the screen the position fetched again\n(FETCH_POS)."},
        "15314": {"synopsis":"The names of keywords $A3 and $A4 in 128 BASIC, last letter with bit 7 set: SPECTRUM, PLAY."},
        "15326": {"synopsis":"Jumps on to the vector at $3C01 (KP_SCAN). Nothing in this ROM comes here."},
        "15329": {"synopsis":"Unused: 30 bytes of $00, then two of $FF, after a jump."},
        "15361": {"synopsis":"Jumps to this ROM's new routines, for code outside it (nothing here calls them): KP_SCAN,\nthen TEST_SCREEN four times."},
        "15376": {"synopsis":"A test picture, only while SPACE and CAPS SHIFT are both held (BREAK); otherwise it returns:\n1. White border, stream 2 (the screen), the upper screen, AT 0,0.\n2. Each of the 64 paper and ink pairs as ATTR_T, eight rows of eight: TEST_TEXT printed once\n   in each (BRIGHT 0, \"19\", BRIGHT 1, \"86\").\n3. The rest of the pixels cleared; the first 256 attributes copied over the next 512.\n4. Interrupts off, then a tone on the speaker forever: $370 half-waves, a pause, again.","comment":"SPACE?"},
        "15381": {"comment":"Not held: return"},
        "15382": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT?"},
        "15387": {"comment":"Not held: return"},
        "15388": {"comment":"White border"},
        "15392": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "15397": {"comment":"TV_FLAG = 0: the upper screen"},
        "15401": {"comment":"AT 0,0"},
        "15408": {"comment":"Eight rows of eight"},
        "15412": {"synopsis":"ATTR_T = paper B - 1, ink D - 1, for the next cell."},
        "15422": {"comment":"ATTR_T"},
        "15425": {"comment":"HL = TEST_TEXT"},
        "15429": {"synopsis":"Prints its eight bytes."},
        "15441": {"comment":"The pixels from $4800 cleared"},
        "15454": {"comment":"The first 256 attributes over the next 512"},
        "15463": {"comment":"Interrupts off: this never ends"},
        "15464": {"synopsis":"$370 half-waves on the speaker (bit 4 of port $FE), each $99 rounds long; then a pause, and\nagain."},
        "15469": {"synopsis":"One half-wave."},
        "15472": {"synopsis":"Its length."},
        "15478": {"comment":"The speaker bit flipped"},
        "15488": {"comment":"The pause: 2 x 65536 rounds"},
        "15491": {"synopsis":"The pause's first 65536 rounds."},
        "15496": {"synopsis":"Its second 65536 rounds."},
        "15503": {"synopsis":"TEST_SCREEN's text: BRIGHT 0, \"19\", BRIGHT 1, \"86\"."},
        "15511": {"synopsis":"Unused: 105 bytes of $00 up to the character set."}
      }
    }
  },
